OL,3,GNEWSA'Extraordinary' Viking items
OL,4,Adeclared as treasure
OL,5,
OL,6,FAn "extraordinary" collection of
OL,7,F1,100-year-old Viking Age artifacts
OL,8,Ffound by metal detectorists on the Isle
OL,9,Fof Man has been declared as treasure.
OL,11,FThe items, uncovered in February by
OL,12,FDaniel Crowe and Rhett Britton, include
OL,13,Fan elaborately decorated sword, three
OL,14,Fbronze brooches, trading weights and
OL,15,Fscales, a bronze ladle and the head of
OL,16,Fan axe.
OL,18,FDating back to AD 900, some of the
OL,19,Fpieces are thought to be from the
OL,20,Fearliest known female Viking Age burial
OL,21,Fon the island.
OL,23,APub: 09-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB IOM NewsC Reg TVF Clean Feed
FL,447,445,260,140,0,100
